# Paths chezmoi removes from the target dir on every apply, relative to ~.
#
# Every entry is a rulesync project-scope output that the --global generate never
# writes, so rulesync's own `delete: true` (scoped to global) can never reclaim it.
# See README.md for the full pipeline.
#
# Do not add .claude/CLAUDE.md here. This file is applied on every apply, but the
# generate script only re-fires on a hash change, so the path would sit missing
# most of the time.

# codexcli rules, project scope. Replaced by ~/.codex/AGENTS.md.
AGENTS.md

# claudecode rules, project scope. Replaced by ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md, which the
# generate script now writes directly instead of through a symlink.
CLAUDE.md
